Hierarchical clustering is of 2 types

1.Agglomerative(Bottom up )technique
2.Divisive(Top down)technique

Note:Both uses distance between the cluster technique

Mechanism:

Linkage Mechanism
A linkage mechanism is a mechanical system made of rigid links
connected by movable joints (like hinges or sliders).
These systems are designed to convert input motion or force into a desired output motion
 or force, often with precision and efficiency.
(Here each of data becomes cluster by itself).

Agglomerative(Bottom up )technique:
1.Every point will be considered as its own cluster
2.Each cluster then merges with most similar cluster in a iterative way
3.This formation happens till single cluster is formed(we will limit the no of clusters needed).

